VERSION: 2.3.2 (06/NOV/2026)
- fixed crashes and hangs when loading damaged design, simulation results and vector table files
- a failed save, for example on a full disk, now keeps the old design file instead of leaving a truncated one


VERSION: 2.3.1 (04/NOV/2026)
- fixed ruler digits being cut off with larger fonts


VERSION: 2.3 (04/NOV/2026)
- fixed crash when opening the Vector Table Setup dialog
- fixed crash when closing the Vector Table Setup and graph windows with the window X button
- fixed results window dropping traces after a bus
- fixed COS clock: clocks 0/2 and 1/3 were identical because the phase shift was applied twice
- fixed initial steady state: every cell now has to converge, and the energy engine starts from the steady state of its own equations
- fixed bistable engine stopping an iteration as soon as the last cell was stable, instead of all cells
- fixed RAMP clock reporting no energy dissipation when a clock landed exactly on its middle value
- fixed energy totals dropping cells closer than 20 nm, and a memory overflow with hidden layers
- fixed crash when saving energy simulation results
- fixed output traces being misplaced when vector table inputs are inactive
- fixed stopped or diverged simulations leaving inactive inputs as normal cells
- fixed memory overflow and trailing zeros in recorded traces, depending on the number of samples
- Runge-Kutta now advances the coherence vector components together
- Ctrl + mouse wheel zooms at the mouse pointer, and Shift + mouse wheel now scrolls sideways
- middle mouse button drag pans in any tool, and Ctrl + middle mouse button drag now draws the zoom box
- generated files are no longer tracked, and configure can be run directly from a fresh clone
- fixed autogen.sh, which is now only needed after changing the build files
- fixed numbers saved with commas on systems that use them, which loaded as wrong values; such files now load correctly
- data files are found relative to the program, so an installed copy can be moved
- added an AppImage build, which GitHub Actions runs for each push and publishes for version tags


